    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Drought analysis",
    "problem": "The widely used Standardized Precipitation Index (SPI) is limited by its coarse monthly time resolution, which prevents the accurate identification of the specific start and end days of drought events, particularly rapidly developing flash droughts.",
    "method": "A multi-scale daily Standardized Precipitation Index (SPI) dataset is developed for mainland China by refining the traditional SPI calculation and applying a gamma probability distribution to daily precipitation data, improving the temporal resolution for monitoring drought events like flash droughts.",
    "task": "The task is to develop an improved, multi-scale daily Standardized Precipitation Index (SPI) dataset for mainland China from 1961 to 2018 to improve the temporal resolution for identifying drought events, especially flash droughts.",
