            "target_entity_instance": "China",
            "target_entity_type": "Country",
            "paragraph": "Drought is the most frequent, complex, chronic, and severe natural disaster worldwide1-3. Drought areas caused by water deficits have significantly spread in the past several decades across China because of climate change 4,5. Northwestern China suffers from severe water resource crises and drought risk.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Drought event",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Northwestern China",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Northwestern China suffers from severe water resource crises and drought risk. The Xinjiang region in northwestern China and the provinces of Hebei and Shanxi in the central part of China experienced more severe droughts, with ATDS values between \u2212155 and \u2212526. The drought in Xinjiang, Qinghai, and other places in northwestern China showed some easement, with a trend greater than 30 (P-value <0.05; Fig. 6b).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": false,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Drought event",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Henan",
            "target_entity_type": "Country_Subdivision",
            "paragraph": "Figure 3 shows that station 53898 (Henan) experienced severe drought disasters in 1965, 1966, 1978, 1986, 1992, and 1993, consistent with the drought disaster events recorded in The Henan Volume of the Chinese Meteorological Dictionary57. According to records, the drought disasters that occurred in Henan Province from 1965 to 1966 were extremely serious, causing rivers and wells to dry up. Among them, the Henan and Yunnan sites have experienced frequent drought disasters since ancient times 38,39.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Drought event",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Yunnan",
            "target_entity_type": "Country_Subdivision",
            "paragraph": "According to The Yunnan Volume of the Chinese Dictionary of Meteorological Disasters58, years of severe drought in Yunnan from 1949 to 2000 include 1963, 1987, 1988, 1992, and 1998. Figure 4 shows that unlike station 53898, extreme drought events at station 56856 in Yunnan Province mostly occurred after 2000. According to The China Meteorological Disaster Yearbook59 from 2004 to 2018, Yunnan Province experienced severe droughts from 2003 to 2004 and from 2009 to 2013, consistent with Fig. 4. Among them, the Henan and Yunnan sites have experienced frequent drought disasters since ancient times 38,39.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": false,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Drought event",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Fujian",
            "target_entity_type": "Country_Subdivision",
            "paragraph": "Previous studies have reported that although the precipitation in Fujian is relatively sufficient, the distribution of precipitation is uneven, and it is also prone to drought2,40\u201342. Compared with the stations in Yunnan and Henan, the station in Fujian Province had plenty of rainfall, but droughts still frequently occurred.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": false,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Drought event",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "central part of China",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The Xinjiang region in northwestern China and the provinces of Hebei and Shanxi in the central part of China experienced more severe droughts, with ATDS values between \u2212155 and \u2212526. Although there was no obvious drought intensification or mitigation in Hebei, Shanxi, and other places in central China, drought events were nevertheless serious.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": false,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Drought event",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "northern China",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "In general, the drought in northern China was more severe than in the south. However, compared with other areas in northern China, the drought in Heilongjiang and Jilin in the northeast was relatively mild (Fig. 6a).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Drought event",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "northeast China",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "However, compared with other areas in northern China, the drought in Heilongjiang and Jilin in the northeast was relatively mild (Fig. 6a). Stations in the northeastern and southwestern regions had a higher frequency of drought events (i.e., higher ATDF values). Drought events at some stations in the northeastern region were not as severe and did not last a long time. However, they occurred frequently (Fig. 8a). The multi-year trend of ATDD also shows that the drought duration at some stations in the southwest, southeast, and northeast regions of China had significantly reduced",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": false,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Drought event",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "southwest regions of China",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The multi-year trend of ATDD also shows that the drought duration at some stations in the southwest, southeast, and northeast regions of China had significantly reduced, while the drought duration at some stations in central and southwestern regions had increased significantly (Fig. 7b). Stations in the northeastern and southwestern regions had a higher frequency of drought events (i.e., higher ATDF values).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Drought event",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "southeast regions of China",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The multi-year trend of ATDD also shows that the drought duration at some stations in the southwest, southeast, and northeast regions of China had significantly reduced, while the drought duration at some stations in central and southwestern regions had increased significantly (Fig. 7b).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
